  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Chapter 323 is titled Start of Three Kings Inheritance. In Shang clan city, Fang Yuan reads that the inheritance has opened on the same date as in his previous life and plans to leave once Shang Xin Ci becomes young master. Now that it has opened, he can finally mass purchase dog enslavement Gu, paper crane Gu, and exploding egg Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_three_kings_inheritance",
        "loc_shang_clan_city",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_shang_xin_ci",
        "gu_dog_enslavement_gu",
        "gu_paper_crane_gu",
        "gu_exploding_egg_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan treats the site as an ancient Gu Master’s blessed land already on the brink of collapse, stripped by the three kings and then pressed further by their remodelled inheritances.",
      "chapters": [
        325
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Shang clan occupies the entrances, Wu clan breaks that blockade, and news that the site is a rank six Gu Immortal blessed land pulls a wider Southern Border wave until even Shang and Wu cannot hold the mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        326
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "From the mountain foot San Cha Mountain rises into three hills like a fork with three tips, and the entrances sit above those peaks.",
      "chapters": [
        339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Entry maps those Gu to the pillars: dog enslavement Gu for King Quan’s yellow pillar, paper crane Gu for King Xin’s blue pillar, and exploding egg Gu for King Bao’s red pillar. The three kings were rank five Gu Masters from Wang clan who rose after finding a rank six Gu Immortal inheritance and wiped Wu clan in three days. King Quan walks enslavement with hound armies, King Xin refinement and information through paper crane lines, and King Bao explosive force.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "king-names-and-entry-map",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_king_quan",
        "char_king_xin",
        "char_king_bao",
        "fac_wang_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 346 is titled Fang Yuan’s first entry into King Quan Inheritance, and that entry takes place inside the Gu Immortal blessed land rather than in the main world.",
      "chapters": [
        346
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "king-names-and-entry-map",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In King Quan Inheritance, difficulty rises sharply every ten rounds of battles. The first ten rounds eliminate most Gu Masters of other paths; later thresholds thin the field until only path elites remain, and the final ten rounds from the ninetieth to the hundredth are treated as a near-impassable wall for anyone below rank five.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the twentieth round, hundred beast kings appear and hundreds to nearly a thousand beasts can attack at once.",
      "chapters": [
        349
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "King Xin Inheritance follows the same every-ten-rounds rise, with hairy men growing smarter and stronger as the rounds advance.",
      "chapters": [
        358
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_king_xin_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan treats undefeated hundred battles Gu as one of the inheritance essences worth taking from this mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_undefeated_hundred_battles_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later orders Feng Tian Yu to bring that Gu from King Xin Inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_tian_yu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Feng Tian Yu delivers it after clearing the hundredth round and receiving King Xin Inheritance: a round limestone-like Gu named undefeated hundred battles Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        389
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rounds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Mu Bai names the same origin: a mysterious Gu Immortal’s blessed land that the three kings inherited and remodelled into an inheritance site.",
      "chapters": [
        374
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_mu_bai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tells Ba Gui that the blessed land came from an ancient strength path Gu Immortal whose dying wish formed the land spirit, and that completing the wish means refining second aperture Gu. Three roaming kids used the blessed land’s resources, became the three kings of the demonic path, failed to break through to rank six, and remodelled the place into the three kings inheritance before dying. They walked refinement, fire, and enslavement path, not strength path. Land spirit Ba Gui is the huge tortoise that awakens as the blessed land nears ruin.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ba_gui",
        "gu_second_aperture_gu",
        "sys_land_spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan succeeds in refining divine travel Gu, the aged land spirit Ba Gui withers and disappears. Immortal essence can no longer be used through it.",
      "chapters": [
        394
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-spirit-fades",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_divine_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan then uses Spring Autumn Cicada and returns to an earlier point still inside the blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        399
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan spreads his wings and flies away. In the collapsing blessed land he refines fixed immortal travel Gu in public as a mortal, then leaves by that Gu with Ba Gui’s immortal essence. The blessed land collapses, winds of assimilation rise, experts flee, and San Cha mountain goes into chaos again.",
      "chapters": [
        405
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "restart-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    }
  ],
